Deep learning pipeline for five-class radar micro-Doppler classification, comparing CNN, CNN–LSTM,
CNN–BiLSTM and CNN–Conv1D–LSTM architectures with targeted time-warping augmentation.

## The work

This project investigates pedestrian and cyclist classification from radar micro-Doppler spectrograms.
The task includes five balanced classes: pedestrian, cyclist, pedestrian plus cyclist, two pedestrians and
two cyclists.
The original 144 × 400 spectrograms are resized to 72 × 200 to reduce memory requirements and training
time. Several deep learning architectures are compared, from convolutional baselines to hybrid models
combining two-dimensional convolutions, one-dimensional temporal filtering and LSTM layers.
Targeted time-warping augmentation is applied to the most difficult double-object classes. The selected
CNN–Conv1D–LSTM model achieves 86.22% test accuracy and approximately 0.862 macro F1 on a
balanced test set of 5,000 samples.

## Technologies

Python, TensorFlow, Keras, NumPy, scikit-learn, Matplotlib.

